  "title": "Establish linked-list baseline with length-only hashing",
  "explanation": "Use string length modulo a prime bucket count as an intentionally poor baseline. Equal-length keys cluster, so tail insertion examines every existing node and counts every occupied node as a collision. Both independent tables preserve duplicate-key records. This first real experiment establishes the space, collision and construction-time baseline before full-string hashing.",
